        "question_text": "<p>The head of the Commonwealth of Nations is the</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The <strong>Commonwealth of Nations</strong> is a political association of mostly former territories of the British Empire. While it operates by consensus and does not have a constitutionally binding leadership structure, it recognises a symbolic <strong>head of the Commonwealth</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>The <strong>Head of the Commonwealth</strong> is a <strong>ceremonial position</strong>, not a political or executive one.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>This role was traditionally held by <strong>Queen Elizabeth II</strong>, and now by <strong>King Charles III</strong>, following her passing.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>It is <strong>not automatically passed</strong> through British monarchy by law, but was reaffirmed by member states.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>",
